# Routing-eval diagnostics, rewritten on every `npm test`. e1-misses.txt stays
# tracked on purpose: it is the regression record of which prompts failed to
# route, so a fix can be seen to hold. last-misses.txt is the baseline report
# from the same run, so tracking it only made every run dirty a tracked file for
# no information a reader could act on.
tests/routing/last-misses.txt

# Local working map, deliberately never tracked. Rebuilt 2026-10-02 after the
# tracked docs/STEAL.md and its self-check gate were removed; the file names
# real upstream repos and working state, so it must stay off the remote. It is
# regenerable from ref/SOURCES.md and `npm test` — nothing tracked depends on it.
notes/STEAL.md

# Holds a credential supplied by whoever runs the benchmark. It was committed
# and pushed once with a hardcoded `||` fallback key, which is how a secret gets
# into a public repo: one `git add -A`. The script now reads the env var only
# and exits when it is unset, but the rule stays so a future edit that re-adds a
# fallback cannot slip in.
tasks/benchmark/run-api.mjs

# Local benchmark scratch, written by run-api.mjs and regenerated per run, like
# the other results-* trees above.
tasks/benchmark/results-api/
